--- Part 5: per-record arithmetic test (NON-tautological) ---
  Over ALL sum-crossings tau=num/D (num=1..floor(D/2), gcd(num,D)=1) with big|q private,
  is fold(flank*num,D) >= ceil(D/14) ALWAYS? (this is the arithmetic statement, not M)
  total sum-crossings checked (flank<big, big privately owns q): 287658
  crossings where fold(flank*num,D) < ceil(D/14): 38536
  => the PER-RECORD arithmetic claim is FALSE if this is >0 (expected): the pair gap
     can be tiny; LRC is saved only because OTHER runners are NOT clear there.
    e.g. ((1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14), 1, 14, 15, 1, 1, 2, (7, 14))
    e.g. ((1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14), 3, 14, 17, 6, 1, 2, (7, 14))
    e.g. ((1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14), 5, 14, 19, 4, 1, 2, (7, 14))
    e.g. ((1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14), 9, 14, 23, 5, 1, 2, (7, 14))
    e.g. ((1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14), 11, 14, 25, 9, 1, 2, (7, 14))
